\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The neutrino moments form a chain. Streaming links each moment to its neighbours; collisions put a rate on each. Non-normality sits only where neighbouring rates differ: on the density--flux link ($k^2\kappa _1^2/3$) and, if shear relaxes at its own rate, on the flux--shear link. Every other link carries none.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:chain}{{1}{3}{The neutrino moments form a chain. Streaming links each moment to its neighbours; collisions put a rate on each. Non-normality sits only where neighbouring rates differ: on the density--flux link ($k^2\kappa _1^2/3$) and, if shear relaxes at its own rate, on the flux--shear link. Every other link carries none}{figure.1}{}}
