\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The surviving share $G$ of the free-streaming shift against decoupling time. Black dots: McCormick's Gaussian runs with $\kappa /H=(\epsilon _{\rm  dec}/\epsilon )^3$; the grey dashed line through them is what a history-blind rule gives for any history. Blue: the kept-sector memory with one weight fitted to the black dots. Orange line: the same form for $\kappa /H=(\epsilon _{\rm  dec}/\epsilon )^6$, computed before any such run and not refitted. Orange diamonds: the new $n=6$ runs C, B and D. Open squares: the broad profile (Test A).}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:G}{{3}{7}{The surviving share $G$ of the free-streaming shift against decoupling time. Black dots: McCormick's Gaussian runs with $\kappa /H=(\epsilon _{\rm dec}/\epsilon )^3$; the grey dashed line through them is what a history-blind rule gives for any history. Blue: the kept-sector memory with one weight fitted to the black dots. Orange line: the same form for $\kappa /H=(\epsilon _{\rm dec}/\epsilon )^6$, computed before any such run and not refitted. Orange diamonds: the new $n=6$ runs C, B and D. Open squares: the broad profile (Test A)}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{The matched pair.}{7}{section*.9}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The three steep-history tests against their kill lines. The shaded band is $\pm 0.08$ around each measurement. Orange: the memory form's prediction, made before the run. Grey circle: the history-blind rule. At $\epsilon _{\rm  dec}=3$ the history-blind rule falls outside the band.}}{8}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:kill}{{4}{8}{The three steep-history tests against their kill lines. The shaded band is $\pm 0.08$ around each measurement. Orange: the memory form's prediction, made before the run. Grey circle: the history-blind rule. At $\epsilon _{\rm dec}=3$ the history-blind rule falls outside the band}{figure.4}{}}
